</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS4.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Post-Hoc Pairwise Comparisons</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the Kruskal-Wallis test indicates whether a difference exists among groups, it does not specify which groups differ from each other.
To resolve this issue, we conducted post-hoc pairwise comparisons using the Mann-Whitney U test, which compares the distributions of two independent groups <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mann and Whitney, 1947</a>)</cite>. This allows us to identify which specific prompt pairs (e.g., Prompt<sub id="S4.SS3.SSS4.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">General</sub> vs. Prompt<sub id="S4.SS3.SSS4.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub">Meaning</sub>) contributed to the overall significant differences.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
